{"event_id":"233fba41-371b-4cc3-b7d2-328112de7002","event_type":"verdict","timestamp_ns":1211190894618709,"wall_time_iso":"2026-10-23T21:12:53.194930+00:00","payload":{"step_id":"pick_hex_red","verdict":"non_conformant","claimed_outcome":null,"clause_results":[{"field":"in_hand_slip","comparison":"lte","threshold":0.02,"observed":0.021774245997197506,"pass":false,"clause_id":null,"source":"instruction"}],"explanation":"Monitor mon_73e54e5a60fc (purpose=clause, threshold=raw_spec.tolerances.grasp_slip_tolerance_m=0.02m for hex_red) fired during/after the pick_hex_red lift: the tcp->hex_red relative translation moved 0.02177m from its reference at grasp time, 1.77mm over the 0.02m tolerance. This is a small margin over threshold; I take it at face value as a measured in-hand slip rather than dismiss it as noise, since the requirement is a hard tolerance with no noise-band carve-out in the spec. Physically this is consistent with the part settling slightly in the RG2 fingers as it transitioned from the guarded-move contact pose into the lift motion. The grasp was not lost (held_object remained hex_red, hex_red_hole insertion is attempted next), but the measured relative displacement exceeds the stated slip tolerance, so I record it as non-conformant on this requirement."},"subscriber_count":2,"seq":15}
